<LegalLayout
  title="AML / BSA Policy"
  description="Public summary of the Trackwise Anti-Money Laundering and Bank Secrecy Act compliance program."
  eyebrow="Compliance"
  effective="2026-05-17"
  lastUpdated="2026-05-17"
>
  <p>
    <strong>Trackwise LLC</strong> is committed to detecting and preventing
    money laundering, terrorist financing, sanctions evasion, and other
    financial crime. Trackwise is registered with FinCEN as a Money Services
    Business (MSB #31000299058422) and operates a written Anti-Money Laundering
    ("AML") / Bank Secrecy Act ("BSA") compliance program.
  </p>

  <h2>1. BSA / AML governance</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The program is owned by our designated <strong>BSA Officer / Chief Compliance Officer</strong>, who reports directly to senior management.</li>
    <li>Written policies and procedures are reviewed at least annually.</li>
    <li>An independent review of the program is conducted at least annually.</li>
    <li>All employees receive AML training appropriate to their role at hire and at least annually.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Risk-based approach</h2>
  <p>
    Trackwise applies a risk-based approach. We assess risk along customer
    type, geography, product, channel, and behavior dimensions, and apply
    proportionate controls.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Customer due diligence (CDD) and KYC / KYB</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Customer identity is verified through document, biometric, and database checks.</li>
    <li>For business customers, beneficial owners with 25% or greater ownership and one control person are identified and verified.</li>
    <li>Enhanced due diligence (EDD) is applied for high-risk customers, including PEPs and customers operating in high-risk geographies.</li>
    <li>We refresh customer information on a risk-based schedule.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Sanctions screening</h2>
  <p>
    We screen customers and counterparties at onboarding and on an ongoing
    basis against:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>OFAC SDN List and Consolidated Sanctions List</li>
    <li>UN consolidated sanctions list</li>
    <li>EU consolidated financial sanctions list</li>
    <li>UK HM Treasury sanctions list</li>
    <li>Country-specific lists where applicable</li>
    <li>PEP and adverse-media data</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Transaction monitoring</h2>
  <p>
    Transactions are monitored using a combination of rule-based and
    behavioral analytics. Alerts are reviewed by trained analysts. The case
    management system maintains a full audit trail.
  </p>

  <h2>6. SAR / CTR reporting</h2>
  <p>
    Trackwise files Suspicious Activity Reports (SARs) and Currency
    Transaction Reports (CTRs) with FinCEN as required by 31 CFR Chapter X.
    We do not tip off subjects of SAR filings.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Recordkeeping</h2>
  <p>
    Trackwise retains BSA / AML records for at least five (5) years from the
    end of the customer relationship or the date of the relevant transaction,
    whichever is later.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Prohibited businesses and activities</h2>
  <p>
    See our <a href="/responsible-use">Responsible Use Policy</a> for the list
    of business types and activities for which Trackwise does not provide
    services.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Cooperation with law enforcement</h2>
  <p>
    Trackwise cooperates with U.S. and foreign law enforcement under
    applicable law. Lawful subpoenas, court orders, and 314(a) / 314(b)
    information-sharing requests should be directed to{' '}
    <a href="mailto:compliance@trackwise.finance">compliance@trackwise.finance</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="mailto:compliance@trackwise.finance">compliance@trackwise.finance</a><br />
    Attn: BSA Officer, Trackwise LLC, 30 N. Gould St., Ste R, Sheridan, WY
    82801, USA
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
